140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 83 0 R
/T (Create a numerical cohort tag for every transaction in the format YYYYMM \(multiplying the year by 100 and adding the month\). Then, groupe the data by customer Name and found the earliest cohort date for each person, labeling it as their first_cohort. Finally, merge this back into the main DataFrame so every transaction knew when that customer first started.)
/E (Create a numerical cohort tag for every transaction in the format YYYYMM \(multiplying the year by 100 and adding the month\). Then, groupe the data by customer Name and found the earliest cohort date for each person, labeling it as their first_cohort. Finally, merge this back into the main DataFrame so every transaction knew when that customer first started.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
