427 0 obj
<<
/Title (Create a numerical cohort tag for every transaction in the format YYYYMM \(multiplying the year by 100 and adding the month\). Then, groupe the data by customer Name and found the earliest cohort date for each person, labeling it as their first_cohort. Finally, merge this back into the main DataFrame so every transaction knew when that customer first started.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 396 0 R
/First 430 0 R
/Last 430 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
428 0 obj
<<
/Title (Calculated the time gap cohort_distance between a customer's transaction month and their very first visit month. Then, built a pivot table counting unique customers \(nunique\) across each cohort row and distance column, and divided each row by its Month 0 base \(cohort_pv[0]\) to turn the raw counts into clear retention percentages.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 397 0 R
/First 431 0 R
/Last 431 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
